From 8b0fcbe38e2bd83ebdad0343c2975d8a67676f41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QIU023 <yiqiaoqiu@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:31:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] kimi_k3: the pipeline stage keeps each attention residual
 block once per rank

The stage hands the model its blocks as a list instead of stacking them
into a fresh leaf, and a hop sends one tensor per block. A received block
is its own receive buffer and a committed block is the model's own tensor,
so the rank cache, the stages' inputs and the sends reference the same
memory, and each block lives once on the rank until the stage that brought
it has run its backward. _assemble_stack, _pack_outgoing_delta and
_split_stack_grad keep their roles on per-block lists; the rank cache, the
routing tables and the release point are unchanged. The model takes and
returns its blocks as a list.

Under the action-list runtime a pending send keeps its tensor allocated, so
a forward send is waited at the stage's own backward of that micro-batch
instead of at the end of the step.
